---
// Kairos Emergency Pedagogy Module 2 with Bernd Ruf, in person in Wilton NH,
// July 2-4, 2027. Copy is Karine's 2026-11-12 announcement as Caitlin forwarded
// it to Jax on 2026-11-14 ("Can you create the event and registration on the
// website"). Groups of three or more, and people also in Renewal Courses or the
// Kairos Summer Residency (July 5-9), arrive with ?coupon=EP2GROUP20 (20% off
// tuition, link only, as on every learn.* checkout).
//
// The checkout lives in src/components/KairosModule2Checkout.astro and is kept
// out of this file on purpose. Left noindex (the site default).
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import KairosModule2Checkout from '../../components/KairosModule2Checkout.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Register: Emergency Pedagogy Module 2 with Bernd Ruf | Center for Anthroposophy"
  portalLabel={null}
  minimal
>
  <header class="registration-head">
    <div class="wrap registration-intro">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow series-link">Kairos Institute · Emergency Pedagogy</p>
        <h1>Module 2: Psychotraumatology II</h1>
        <p class="cohort">Psychotraumatology of Childhood and Adolescence: helping schools become trauma-informed, trauma-responsive, and trauma-recovering</p>
        <p class="intro-copy">
          Three days in person with Bernd Ruf. This module explores how traumatic experiences
          affect human development, from prenatal life through adolescence, and how
          trauma-responsive education can support recovery and renewed developmental growth.
        </p>
        <p class="course-details">Friday to Sunday, July 2–4, 2027</p>
        <p class="course-format">In person · Wilton, New Hampshire · Tuition $425 · EPWB certificate $45 (optional)</p>
        <a class="course-link" href="#registration-form">See registration details <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="when-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">When and where</p>
        <ol class="seminar-list">
          <li>
            <span class="seminar-no">Dates</span>
            <strong>July 2–4, 2027</strong>
            <span class="seminar-parts">The daily schedule will be sent to registrants.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="seminar-no">Place</span>
            <strong>Wilton, New Hampshire</strong>
            <span class="seminar-parts">In person</span>
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p class="when-note">Group discount: 20% off tuition for groups of three or more, and for participants
          also attending Renewal Courses or the Kairos Summer Residency (July 5–9). Write to the office for the group link.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="wrap module-section" aria-labelledby="covers-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">What the module covers</p>
    <h2 id="covers-title">Trauma across childhood and adolescence</h2>
    <p>Participants deepen their understanding of how trauma can interrupt developmental
      processes, affect attachment, sensory development, rhythm, and identity formation, and
      influence a child’s capacity to learn and thrive.</p>
    <ul class="cert-list">
      <li>Trauma and human development, including the developmental perspectives of Rudolf Steiner and Jean Piaget.</li>
      <li>Prenatal trauma and its possible developmental consequences.</li>
      <li>Trauma in early childhood: attachment, sensory development, and healthy development.</li>
      <li>Trauma during the school years: rhythm, sleep, and nervous system regulation.</li>
      <li>Trauma in adolescence: puberty, identity formation, and developmental challenges.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Through pedagogical perspectives and practical exploration, participants learn how
      trauma-responsive education can support recovery. Experiential workshop: eurythmy, and
      movement and games.</p>
    <p>The Emergency Pedagogy training has twelve modules, which may be taken as a complete program
      or individually. Modules 1 and 2 provide the foundation; the rest may be taken in any order.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap facilitator-welcome" aria-labelledby="speaker-title">
    <img class="facilitator-photo" src="/images/51b35b4e70-portrait-of-bernd-ruf-300x300.jpg"
      alt="Portrait of Bernd Ruf."
      width="150" height="150" loading="lazy" />
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Founder, Parzival School &amp; Emergency Pedagogy</p>
      <h2 id="speaker-title">Bernd Ruf</h2>
      <p>Bernd Ruf is the founder of the worldwide emergency pedagogy crisis intervention centre
        based in Karlsruhe, Germany, from which skilled teams are sent to help traumatised
        children in places of war and ecological disaster. He is the author of
        <em>Educating Traumatized Children</em>.</p>
      <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-top: 28px;">Certificates</p>
      <p>There are two, and they are separate things.</p>
      <ul class="cert-list">
        <li><strong>Certificate of Completion</strong>, issued by the Center for Anthroposophy. No cost.</li>
        <li><strong>Module 2 Certificate</strong>, issued by Emergency Pedagogy Without Borders (EPWB), $45. The
          twelve modules together build toward the EPWB Diploma in International Crisis Intervention.
          Add it when you register; tuition discounts do not apply to it. The Kairos team will
          request your date of birth separately and arrange the certificate through EPWB after the
          module has been taught.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="welcome-credit">Module 2 is part of the Kairos Institute’s Emergency Pedagogy series
        with Bernd Ruf. Questions about the module, or about a certificate, can go to Lisl Hofer,
        Manager of the Kairos Institute, at
        <a href="mailto:lisl@centerforanthroposophy.org">lisl@centerforanthroposophy.org</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <KairosModule2Checkout program="kairos-ep-module-2-2027" />
</Base>

<style>
  .registration-head {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: linear-gradient(120deg, rgba(176, 136, 16, 0.12), transparent 62%);
    padding: 56px 0 48px;
  }
  .registration-intro {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(0, 0.8fr);
    gap: 48px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .registration-head h1 {
    font-size: clamp(36px, 4.6vw, 58px);
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    margin-top: 6px;
  }
  .series-link { color: var(--green-ink); }
  .cohort {
    color: var(--gold);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 18px;
    letter-spacing: 0.035em;
    margin-top: 14px;
  }
  .intro-copy { color: var(--soft); font-size: 20px; max-width: 52ch; margin-top: 24px; }
  .course-details { font: 600 16px/1.7 var(--sans); margin-top: 24px; }
  .course-format { color: var(--soft); font: 14px/1.7 var(--sans); margin-top: 8px; }
  .course-link { display: inline-flex; gap: 16px; margin-top: 24px; color: var(--green-ink); font: 600 15px var(--sans); text-underline-offset: 5px; }
  .course-link:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--green); outline-offset: 6px; }
  .when-card { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 3px solid var(--gold); background: var(--raised); padding: 26px 28px; min-width: 0; }
  .seminar-list { list-style: none; margin: 14px 0 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 18px; }
  .seminar-list li { display: grid; gap: 2px; }
  .cert-list { margin: 14px 0 0; padding-left: 1.2em; }
  .cert-list li { margin-top: 8px; max-width: 68ch; }
  .module-section { padding-top: 40px; padding-bottom: 40px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .module-section h2 { font-size: clamp(25px, 3vw, 34px); margin: 8px 0 16px; }
  .module-section p { max-width: 68ch; margin-top: 12px; }
  .seminar-no { color: var(--gold); font: 11px var(--sans); letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .seminar-list strong { font-size: 19px; font-weight: 600; }
  .seminar-parts { color: var(--soft); font: 14px/1.7 var(--sans); }
  .when-note { color: var(--soft); font: 13px/1.6 var(--sans); margin-top: 16px; }
  .facilitator-welcome { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 150px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 36px; align-items: start; padding-top: 48px; padding-bottom: 48px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .facilitator-photo { width: 150px; height: 150px; border-radius: 50%; object-fit: cover; }
  .facilitator-welcome h2 { font-size: clamp(25px, 3vw, 34px); margin: 8px 0 16px; }
  .facilitator-welcome p { max-width: 68ch; margin-top: 12px; }
  .welcome-credit { color: var(--soft); font: 14px/1.6 var(--sans); margin-top: 20px; }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .registration-intro { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 22px; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .registration-head { padding: 38px 0 34px; }
    .facilitator-welcome { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 22px; padding-top: 32px; padding-bottom: 32px; }
    .facilitator-photo { width: 110px; height: 110px; }
  }
</style>
